# Signals (roadmap os-server.md P10): init starts tests/posix/signal.c
# (TEST_POSIX_SIGNAL), whose handlers run in a busy loop, in a blocked read
# (EINTR; and made again, SA_RESTART), in a sleep, nested, after being
# blocked and pending, for sigsuspend, pause and alarm; faults reach
# handlers; SIG_IGN, SIGCHLD, SIGTERM's and SIGKILL's default actions; and
# a frame its handler spoilt ends its process with SIGSEGV.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_SIGNAL
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 240
# DOSBox-X stops itself at an IRET with NT whose TSS is not busy, where a
# 286 raises #TS (docs/emulators.md).
emulators: bochs mame
---
signal: a handler in a busy loop (3): exit 3
signal: a read broken off, EINTR (4): exit 4
signal: a read made again, SA_RESTART (5): exit 5
signal: a sleep broken off, the seconds left (6): exit 6
signal: nested (12/): 12/
signal: blocked: ran 0, pending 1 (0 1)
signal: unblocked: ran 1 (1)
signal: sigsuspend: -1, EINTR 1, ran 1 (-1 1 1)
signal: its child (0): exit 0
signal: pause: -1, EINTR 1, SIGALRM 1 (-1 1 1)
signal: alarm: 5 seconds left (5): 5
signal: nanosleep: 5 ticks or more (1): 1
signal: SIGUSR2 ignored: alive
signal: a child for SIGCHLD (0): exit 0
signal: SIGCHLD (1): 1
signal: #UD to its handler (SIGILL 4): exit 4
signal: #GP to its handler (SIGSEGV 11): exit 11
signal: #DE to its handler (SIGFPE 8): exit 8
signal: SIGTERM's default action (15): signal 15
signal: SIGKILL, never caught (9): signal 9
signal: a spoilt frame (SIGSEGV 11): signal 11
signal: IOPL and NT asked for: IOPL 0 (0), NT 1
signal: its own IRET with NT (SIGSEGV 11): signal 11
signal: done
